---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/kit/PageHeader.astro";
import DraftNotice from "../components/kit/DraftNotice.astro";
import PrivacyChoice from "../components/site/PrivacyChoice.astro";

export const prerender = true;

/*
 * DRAFT, NOT LEGAL ADVICE. Needs review by a Philippine lawyer before launch.
 * Written against the Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173) and its IRR.
 * Confirm before launch:
 *   - the legal entity name and address (the business isn't registered yet)
 *   - whether a Data Protection Officer must be registered with the NPC
 *   - the retention periods below
 *   - the lawful basis for each purpose
 *   - that the processors listed match what's deployed
 * Several statements are commitments the product must keep (consent gating
 * of usage stats, location staying on the device, the response window).
 */
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How Visita handles personal data under the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173).">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10">
    <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy policy" lede="How Visita handles personal data, written for the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (RA 10173)." />
    <div class="prose-visita">
      <DraftNotice>This policy is a working draft and hasn't been reviewed by a lawyer yet. It will be finalised before public launch.</DraftNotice>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Visita is a cafe discovery service in Cagayan de Oro, Philippines. Under RA 10173 we are the personal information controller for the data described here.
        Our registered business name and address will be published here once registration is complete. Data protection contact: <strong>privacy@visita.ph</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect, and why</h2>

      <h3>Your account</h3>
      <p>
        You sign in with Google. We receive your name, email address and profile photo from Google, and give your account an identifier. We use these to run your
        account and to show your name beside reviews you publish. We never see your Google password.
      </p>

      <h3>Reviews and photos</h3>
      <p>
        When you write a review we store your rating, your text and any photo you add, and publish them on the cafe's page with your display name. Only upload photos
        you took yourself, and leave other people's personal details out of your reviews.
      </p>

      <h3>Saved and recently viewed cafes</h3>
      <p>Cafes you save are stored with your account so they follow you across devices. Recently viewed cafes are kept on your device only.</p>

      <h3>Your location</h3>
      <p>
        If you allow it, your browser tells Visita your approximate location so we can show how far cafes are. This stays on your device: it isn't sent to us or
        stored. It's optional, and everything else works without it.
      </p>

      <h3>Usage statistics, only if you allow them</h3>
      <p>
        If you choose "Allow usage stats" on the privacy notice, we count things like page visits, walkthrough opens, taps on "Get directions", and which searches
        and filters led to a cafe. Cafe owners see these as totals for their own listing, never as individuals. We use our own first-party measurement: no
        advertising trackers and no third-party analytics. If you choose "Essential only", none of this is recorded. You can change your choice here at any
        time:
      </p>
      <PrivacyChoice />

      <h3>Scan requests</h3>
      <p>
        When you tap "I want to see inside" on a cafe that isn't scanned yet, we record which cafe, a random code for this browser, and a one-way code worked out
        from your network address for that day. The network code is used only to stop automated requests, can't be turned back into your address, and is erased
        after two days.
      </p>

      <h3>Venue owners</h3>
      <p>
        If you register as a venue owner, we also collect your contact details, details of the venue, and what's needed to confirm you manage it. We keep records of
        subscription payments you make to us.
      </p>

      <h3>Directions</h3>
      <p>
        "Get directions" opens Google Maps or Apple Maps with the cafe as the destination. From that point the maps provider's own privacy policy applies. We don't
        receive anything back from them.
      </p>

      <h3>On your device</h3>
      <p>
        We store a sign-in session, your privacy choice, your saved and recently viewed cafes, and any review you're still writing in your browser. These are needed for the site to work and aren't used to
        track you across other sites.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Legal bases</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Consent:</strong> usage statistics and location. You can change your mind at any time with the choice under "Usage statistics" above, or in your browser's location settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Contract:</strong> running your account and, for venue owners, your listing and subscription.</li>
        <li><strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> keeping the service secure, preventing abuse, and moderating reviews.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>We don't sell personal data. We use these service providers to run Visita, and they process data only on our instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong>: database and sign-in.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, and storage of scans and photos.</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong>: sign-in with your Google account.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may disclose data where Philippine law or a lawful order requires it.</p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>Kept for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Your account</td><td>While your account is open, then deleted within 30 days of closing it, unless the law requires longer</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Published reviews and photos</td><td>Until you delete them or close your account</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Usage statistics</td><td>24 months, then kept only as totals that identify no one</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Network code on scan requests</td><td>2 days</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Venue owner and payment records</td><td>As long as the listing is active, then as required for tax and accounting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Data on your device</td><td>Until you clear your browser's data for this site</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>6. Your rights under RA 10173</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>To be informed</strong> whether and why we process your data.</li>
        <li><strong>To access</strong> a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
        <li><strong>To correct</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
        <li><strong>To erasure or blocking</strong> where data is no longer needed, was unlawfully obtained, or you withdraw consent.</li>
        <li><strong>To data portability</strong>, in a commonly used electronic format.</li>
        <li><strong>To object</strong> to processing, including processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
        <li><strong>To damages</strong> for harm caused by inaccurate, incomplete or unlawfully obtained data.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <strong>privacy@visita.ph</strong> with enough detail for us to find the data. We aim to reply within 15 working days. If you're not satisfied, you can
        complain to the <a href="https://privacy.gov.ph" rel="noopener">National Privacy Commission</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Security</h2>
      <p>
        Visita is served over HTTPS, and access to stored data is limited by account and role. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal data,
        we'll notify you and the National Privacy Commission as RA 10173 requires.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children</h2>
      <p>Visita isn't meant for children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their data. If you think a child has given us data, contact us and we'll delete it.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We'll update this policy as Visita changes, and show the date of the latest revision at the top.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
